ion, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{2x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $13\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}=-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))-2(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))=13\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(3\\beta -2\\alpha )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+(-3\\alpha -2\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)=13\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3\\beta -2\\alpha =13\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)) \\\\ -3\\alpha -2\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-2,\\beta =3.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{2x}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the constant $A$ using the initial conditions.\n\nSubstituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{2\\cdot 0}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0) & =2 \\\\ A-2-0 & =2 \\\\ A & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=4{e}^{2x}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060230/state.json" "file_sha256" "093dd508ec67fcec3e70eef6de24f6b2832b8b54d9a7733396276bf275173f55"} {"question" "q-333388" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060230/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4e71a15a2030c484d9f2413bae029cea7c1017bcf220c4de380e8eafff14ff1a"} {"question" "q-333388" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060230/state.json" "file_sha256" "093dd508ec67fcec3e70eef6de24f6b2832b8b54d9a7733396276bf275173f55"} {"question" "q-333388" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4e^{2x}-2\\cos(3x)+3\\sin(3x)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060230/state.json" "file_sha256" "093dd508ec67fcec3e70eef6de24f6b2832b8b54d9a7733396276bf275173f55"} {"question" "q-333396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4y=25\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\,y(0)=2\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+4y=25\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\n$$\n\nhas the complementary solution ${y}_{c}=A{e}^{-4x},$ solve the initial value problem.\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060230/state.json" "file_sha256" "093dd508ec67fcec3e70eef6de24f6b2832b8b54d9a7733396276bf275173f55"} {"question" "q-333396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nTo find the complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}^{′}+4{y}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we find that the complementary solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A{e}^{-4x}\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $25\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}^{′}=-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha ,$ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))+4(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))=25\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(3\\beta +4\\alpha )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+(-3\\alpha +4\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)=25\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3\\beta +4\\alpha =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)) \\\\ -3\\alpha +4\\beta =25\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-3,\\beta =4.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-4x}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nNow, we can find the constant $A$ using the initial conditions.\n\nSubstituting $y(0)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{e}^{-4\\cdot 0}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0)+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0) & =2 \\\\ A-3-0 & =2 \\\\ A & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=5{e}^{-4x}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060230/state.json" "file_sha256" "093dd508ec67fcec3e70eef6de24f6b2832b8b54d9a7733396276bf275173f55"} {"question" "q-333396" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060230/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4e71a15a2030c484d9f2413bae029cea7c1017bcf220c4de380e8eafff14ff1a"} {"question" "q-333396" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14060230/state.json" "file_sha256" "093dd508ec67fcec3e70eef6de24f6b2832b8b54d9a7733396276bf275173f55"} {"question" "q-333396" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5e^{-4x}-3\\cos(3x)+4\\sin(3x)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differentia